ath but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 activ histori 2026 06 25 diana task creat open\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee462b568a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"7a5b7d5f97fb04a1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3895338280622975, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2045334229461394, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82120144, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee462b568a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:12\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0973008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"b1a90ff76c3fb32a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29482546384995634, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09599800549993766, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7587562, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0973008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:09\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement an OCR-based fallback for documents that lack a usable native text layer (WS-01). A Tesseract proof-of-concept succeeded, but profiling found that a page-serial Tesseract loop was a latency bottleneck; Charlie implemented a per-page multiprocessing pool and retuned OCR confidence thresholds afterward. Diana has begun wiring the OCR fallback output into the scan pipeline while the parallelization work remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- OCR fallback triggers correctly when native text extraction is unavailable.\\n\\n- Per-page multiprocessing and confidence-threshold tuning integrate cleanly with the scan pipeline (integration in progress; task remains Active).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement an OCR-based fallback for documents that lack a usable native text layer (WS-01). A Tesseract proof-of-concept succeeded, but profiling found that a page-serial Tesseract loop was a latency bottleneck; Charlie implemented a per-page multiprocessing pool and retuned OCR confidence thresholds afterward. Diana has begun wiring the OCR fallback output into the scan pipeline while the parallelization work remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\