completion. On 2026-08-11 Diana verified those hooks: ephemeral OCR temps were removed after both failure and successful completion paths.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-40\\n\\n# Ephemeral OCR Temp Cleanup — Verification Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2040\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n*Retrospective note: this summarizes the 2026-08-11 secure-deletion confirmation for T025, written up today.*\\n\\nOCR fallback leaves temporary files on disk. Those files must not survive after a failed page or after a successful completion.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nCompleted. Secure deletion of ephemeral OCR temps is confirmed for the paths covered by this check. This report does not raise a separate open remanence finding beyond that confirmation.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 40 ephemer ocr temp cleanup verif report owner diana document key doc 2040 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect note this summar the 2026 08 11 secur delet confirm for t025 written up today ocr fallback leaf temporari file on disk those file must not surviv after a fail page or after a success complet confirm earlier work trace ocr temp creation site and ad cleanup hook on failur and complet on 2026 08 11 diana verifi those hook ephemer ocr temp were remov after both failur and success complet path sourc id src gdoc 40 ephemer ocr temp cleanup verif report owner diana document key doc 2040 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect note this summar the 2026 08 11 secur delet confirm for t025 written up today ocr fallback leaf temporari file on disk those file must not surviv after a fail page or after a success complet result complet secur delet of ephemer ocr temp is confirm for the path cover by this check this report doe not rais a separ open reman find beyond that confirm\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee8496fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"b3c426dc4f33fdd3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24635616039154015, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.037994014845057385, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7325345, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee8496fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 832, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:15\", \"token_count\": 305, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"7d969f7c78a9200e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24565325282394967, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04749251831992811, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7080283, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfac6fc8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:23\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-35\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-35\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-35\\n\\n**Title**: Delete ephemeral OCR temp files after failure/completion\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnsure ephemeral OCR temp files are cleaned up and don't persist after processing failures. Cleanup hooks were added and confirmed to securely delete ephemeral OCR temp files after both failure and completion paths.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-35\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-35\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-35\\n\\n**Title**: Delete ephemeral OCR temp files after failure/completion\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2