 \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-10-Policy-Matrix.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eed444228a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-10-Policy-Matrix.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-10-Policy-Matrix.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 466, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:09\", \"token_count\": 210, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- **2026-06-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to define fail-closed error handling for the batch engine.*\\n\\n- **2026-06-15**: Bob - Completion (Completed)\\n\\n - *Completed the fail-closed implementation.*\\n\\n- **2026-07-16**: Diana - QA validates fail-closed (no output file; secure temp deletion) (Completed)\\n\\n - *QA confirmed no output file on failure and secure temp-file deletion, ahead of encryption/offline gates depending on this behavior.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2026 06 08 alic task creat open task open to defin fail close error handl for the batch engin 2026 06 15 bob complet complet complet the fail close implement 2026 07 16 diana qa valid fail close no output file secur temp delet complet qa confirm no output file on failur and secur temp file delet ahead of encrypt offlin gate depend on this behavior\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee50b5308a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"id\": \"cbb9deb89e339811\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24542501195641384, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04614915993773406, \"vector_similarity\": 0.710402, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee50b5308a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1283, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:04\", \"token_count\": 638, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement an OCR-based fallback for documents that lack a usable native text layer (WS-01). A Tesseract proof-of-concept succeeded, but profiling found that a page-serial Tesseract loop was a latency bottleneck; Charlie implemented a per-page multiprocessing pool and retuned OCR confidence thresholds afterward. Diana has begun wiring the OCR fallback output into the scan pipeline while the parallelization work remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- OCR fallback triggers correctly when native text extraction is unavailable.\\n\\n- Per-page multiprocessing and confidence-threshold tuning integrate cleanly with the scan pipeline (integration in progress; task remains Active).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement an OCR-based fallback for documents that lack a usable native text layer (WS-01). A Tesseract proof-of-concept succeeded, but profiling found that a page-serial Tesseract loop was a latency bottleneck; Charlie implemented a per-page multiprocessing pool and retuned OCR confidence thresholds afterward. Diana has begun wiring the OCR fallback output into the scan pipeline while the parallelization work remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-18\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-18\\n\\n**Title**: OCR Fallback for Non-Text-Layer Documents\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-24\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-24**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 18 sourc id src cu ciph 18 task id ciph 18 titl ocr fallback for non text layer document status activ assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 24 descript implement an ocr base fallback for document that lack a usabl nativ text layer w 01 a tesseract proof of concept succeed but profil found that a page serial tesseract loop wa a latenc bottleneck charli implement a per page multiprocess pool and retun ocr confid threshold afterward diana ha begun wire the ocr fallback output into the scan pipelin while the parallel work remain activ clickup task ciph 18 sourc id src cu ciph 18 task id ciph 18 titl ocr fallback for non text layer document status activ assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 24 accept criterion ocr fallback trigger correct when nativ text extract is unavail per page multiprocess and confid threshold tune integr clean with the scan pipelin integr in progress task remain activ clickup task ciph 18 sourc id src cu ciph 18 task id ciph 18 titl ocr fallback for non text layer document status activ assigne charli prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 24 descript i